  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Query Rewriting: HyDE, Multi-Query, and Decomposition Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `MockLLM` - the deterministic stand-in described above."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `HyDERewriter` - calls the LLM to write the hypothetical document, returns the rewriter output as `RewriteResult` with the hypothetical text and the query the retriever should use."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `MultiQueryRewriter` - calls the LLM for N paraphrases, returns a list of queries."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `DecomposeRewriter` - calls the LLM to decompose, returns sub-questions."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `retrieve_with_rewriter` - takes a rewriter and a retriever, runs the rewrites, fuses the results."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A demo that runs the three rewriters on a fixture and prints which strategy returned the gold answer document first."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The retriever shape is reused from lesson 65 (hybrid BM25 + dense). The fusion is the same RRF. The only new shape is the rewriter interface, which is small."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The output is a per-strategy ranking and a final summary. HyDE wins on the phrasing-mismatched query. Multi-query wins on the paraphrase-variance query. Decomposition wins on the multi-topic query. The fallback (no rewriter) loses on at least one of the three."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Implement RAG-Fusion (a 2024 variant of multi-query) where the rewriter's paraphrases are intentionally diverse, then the rerank step (lesson 66) picks the final list.\n2. Add a fourth strategy: step-back prompting (ask the LLM for the more general question, retrieve on that, then narrow). Compare on the fixture.\n3. Train the decomposer to recognize atomic queries by adding a \"is the question atomic\" head. Measure the over-split rate before and after.\n4. Replace the mock LLM with a real model call. Measure the latency-per-strategy on your stack.\n5. Add a confidence score per rewrite. Drop rewrites below the threshold. Measure the impact on recall."
      ]
    }
  ],
